    "sentence_translations": [
      "The character for “happiness” turned upside down",
      "",
      "In China, you may discover that a lot of places have the character for “happiness” above their door.",
      "If you look closely, you will discover that these “happiness” characters are all put up upside down.",
      "Chinese people like to put up the “happiness” character during New Year's, but why do they put them upside down?",
      "",
      "First take the characters for “happiness” and “reverse” and read them together: “happiness reversed”.",
      "Did you think of anything?",
      "The character for “reverse” is pronounced like the character for “arrival”, so “happiness reversed” is read the same as “happiness arrives”.",
      "Putting the “happiness” character upside down therefore means that happiness will arrive."
    ]
  }
